<title>USA: Greyhound stake cut by Canadian firm.</title>
<headline>Greyhound stake cut by Canadian firm.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Connor Clark &amp; Co Ltd, a Toronto, Ontario,-based investment adviser, said Monday it reduced its stake in Greyhound Lines Inc to 6.1 percent or 3,544,637 common shares.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, the firm said it sold a net of 382,235 shares of Greyhound between November 12 and January 6.</p>
<p>Transactions included the sale of 387,335 shares between at prices ranging from $3.43 to $4.35 a share and the purchase of 5,100 shares for $3.70 to $4.47 a share.</p>
</text>
